                        "recommendationid": "41530459",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198008299258",
                            "num_reviews": 378,
                            "playtime_forever": 82,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 82,
                            "last_played": 1523913417
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Picked this up in a bundle, didn’t know what to expect going in. 1.5 hours later, I had to pull myself out - it’s strangely addicting! You play as the operator of a giant UFO, fitted with various weapons and power ups. Some notable weapons: Drop tripod walkers (surface attack vehicles) into the play field, a black hole that sucks nearby buildings into it, and lock-on targeting blasters. Each planet you go against is basically the same (at least the first four have been) other than one or two unique defensive capabilities. There’s some strategy here, to obliterate the outer city blocks, but not take focus away from the city centers for too long, otherwise you’re doomed to fail against their defenses.\n\nGraphics are fine, controls are straightforward, and it runs smooth and stable. I wouldn’t buy it for the full asking price, but am really happy to have it for the price I paid! Thumbs up!",
